6), and 'invalid-spec' (line 216) — all land a criterion in `withheld`.","The plan consumes this contract ('CONSUMES the runner's verdict') but only names the emitter's field (skipped_unbalanced) by its exact key, not the runner's."],"finding":"Trigger #1's failure signal names 'the admission runner's per-criterion reproduction-failure result', but the runner exposes no field by that name; reproduction failures surface as AdmissionSummary.withheld entries paired with DriftEntry.reason strings, and `withheld` also carries non-reproduction reasons ('invalid-spec', 'unbalanced'). Which drift-reason value(s) count as a counter-incrementing reproduction failure is not pinned to the actual enum vocabulary the runner emits.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"feae726191e20f6ec","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → Quarantine breaker, trigger #1 ('the admission runner's per-criterion reproduction-failure result')","norm_id":"n9b51cd7765947fa3","priority":0.67,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A criterion withheld with reason 'invalid-spec' — does the loop increment the breaker counter, treat it like a reproduction failure, or ignore it? The plan does not say.","Executor reads AdmissionSummary and must guess which drift-reason values map to trigger #1."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State that a run fails for a criterion when it appears in AdmissionSummary.withheld with a DriftEntry.reason in {non-reproducing, unbalanced}, plus the emitter's skipped_unbalanced, and specify whether 'invalid-spec' counts.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.85,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the un-minable-reason wording with parent 65dd: note that the two leaf drift reasons (not-inline-admissible / container-material-unrecoverable) are a refinement of the parent's single 'finder not inline-runnable' class, delivering the same quarantine-both-classes behavior — or align the terminology so the parent/leaf framing reads consistently.","cohort":["G7"],"criteria":["G7"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.85,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Parent 65dd Approach: 'Both non-inline classes still carry a cohort tag, so the selector EXCLUDES them from inline mining and the self-healing loop files an unreliable-criterion: ticket (reason: finder not inline-runnable) for each'","Leaf: 'These are two reasons, NOT one \"not inline-runnable\" class — the loop does not re-derive inline-runnability; it CONSUMES the runner's verdict'","Parent Child decomposition: 'residual gaps + container/ISF criteria -> the self-healing loop, which files the unreliable-criterion: tickets' — the deliverable (quarantine both classes) is preserved, so this is a cosmetic reason-labeling refinement, not a contract contradiction"],"finding":"The leaf reframes the parent's single 'finder not inline-runnable' un-minable reason as two distinct reasons ('not-inline-admissible' and 'container-material-unrecoverable'), explicitly stating 'These are two reasons, NOT one not-inline-runnable class' — a wording-level mismatch against the parent's Approach clause, though the delivered behavior (quarantine both container/ISF classes on first encounter) is identical to the parent's contract.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f37447c964d26248c","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Leaf 'Quarantine breaker' trigger #2 vs parent 65dd Approach ('the self-healing loop files an unreliable-criterion: ticket (reason: finder not inline-runnable) for each')","norm_id":"nc78f4e1a90c585d8","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reader cross-referencing the parent's 'finder not inline-runnable' single-reason label against the leaf's two distinct drift reasons may perceive a divergence where the outcome is actually identical."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"na","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the ledger file's lifecycle: whether cumulative-actual re-checks scope the $25 cap per-interval or lifetime, and whether/how the ledger file is pruned or rolled so it does not accumulate indefinitely.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Each run pre-flights through ledger.reserve(..., cap_usd=25.0) against the loop's own ledger'","'the loop's own ledger file' (Scope) — no retire/pruning path stated","Counter and gap-list retirement are specified ('counter RESETS to zero when the criterion becomes covered'; 'work shrinks monotonically to zero') but the ledger file's lifecycle end is not"],"finding":"The loop introduces its own persistent ledger file as new shared state but specifies no RETIRE/cleanup path for it; unlike the failure counter (which resets on coverage/ticket-close) and the gap list (which shrinks to zero), the ledger file appears to accumulate spend records indefinitely across intervals with no stated bound or pruning.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc5bf2b92ac9eab69","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'Unattended spend bound + failure disposition' and Scope ('the loop's own ledger file')","norm_id":"n33c8dad56ab04e87","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Over many intervals the loop's ledger file grows with each finalize()/reserve record; without a retire path it leaks/accumulates, and it is unclear whether cumulative-actual re-checks are per-interval or all-time (which changes whether the $25 cap is per-interval or lifetime)."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the failure disposition of the ticket-creation write arm (retryable/transient vs fatal) and what happens to the consecutive-failure counter if the write fails after the threshold is reached.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.failure-disposition-contract"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.6525,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["'On the third consecutive such run the loop files the ticket' and 'it files the ticket immediately' — the file-ticket operation is a new failure arm","BudgetExceeded arm carries an explicit disposition ('FATAL, non-retryable') but the ticket-write arm carries none","'Creation is IDEMPOTENT — filed only when no OPEN ticket with that exact title exists' addresses duplicates, not write-failure disposition"],"finding":"The plan states dispositions for reproduction failure (not-an-error, continue), skipped_unbalanced (counter increment), and the ledger BudgetExceeded arm (FATAL, non-retryable), but it does not state the failure disposition of the ticket-creation write itself — if filing the `unreliable-criterion:` ticket fails (store write error, transient I/O), the plan does not say whether the run treats that as retryable/transient or fatal, nor what happens to the consecutive-failure counter that triggered it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0c547eabe140c2d3","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'Quarantine breaker' triggers and 'the idempotent unreliable-criterion: ticket creation'","norm_id":"ndd4ab589931e6791","priority":0.2475,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A transient store write failure during ticket creation leaves the criterion un-quarantined but the counter possibly at 3; on the next run, unclear whether it retries the file, resets, or re-increments — the disposition when the ticket write itself fails is unstated."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State whether the 3-consecutive-failure threshold is configurable (mirroring the interval's 'default N' treatment) and capture the recurring repair-loop / quarantine-breaker decision in an ADR or AGENTS.md note.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T5e"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["'On the third consecutive such run the loop files the ticket' — the count 3 is stated as a literal with no configurability note, unlike the interval which is 'configurable interval (default 30 days)'.","The plan introduces a new cross-component pipeline stage (selector+emitter+runner+ledger+tickets wiring) but records no ADR/design-doc update; it only references sibling a5bf's pattern inline."],"finding":"The 3-consecutive-failure quarantine threshold is asserted as a hardcoded constant with no statement that it is configurable, and the new recurring repair-loop pipeline stage / quarantine-breaker pattern is not captured in an ADR or AGENTS.md note beyond the inline reference to sibling a5bf.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f62789d3fb2a44da6","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'Quarantine breaker' trigger #1; Scope","norm_id":"n094194783fdf458d","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An operator later wants a stricter (2) or looser (5) failure threshold and must edit code rather than config.","A future maintainer reads the codebase and cannot find a captured decision record for the recurring-loop / quarantine-ticket pattern."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Express the failure threshold as a configured default (e.g. 'consecutive-failure threshold, default 3') and add a one-paragraph ADR/AGENTS.md entry describing the loop, its triggers, and its ledger, cross-linking sibling a5bf.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5714,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifa